d \\( ML = BL \\) (from the properties of the isosceles trapezoid):\n   \\[\n   CL < BL + BL\n   \\]\n\n8. Simplify the inequality:\n   \\[\n   CL < 2BL\n   \\]\n\n9. Therefore, the proof concludes that:\n   \\[\n   CL < 2BL\n   \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{CL < 2BL}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Given that \\(\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{2}{y} + \\frac{3}{z} = 0\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{6}{y} - \\frac{5}{z} = 0\\), find the value of \\(P = \\frac{x}{y} + \\frac{y}{z} + \\frac{z}{x}\\).", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, so I need to find the value of P, which is equal to x/y + y/z + z/x, given these two equations involving reciprocals of x, y, and z. Let me start by writing down the equations again to make sure I have them right:\n\n1/x + 2/y + 3/z = 0  ...(1)\n\n1/x - 6/y - 5/z = 0  ...(2)\n\nHmm, both equations are equal to zero. Maybe I can subtract one equation from the other to eliminate some terms? Let me see. If I subtract equation (2) from equation (1), what happens?\n\nLeft side: (1/x + 2/y + 3/z) - (1/x - 6/y - 5/z) = 0 - 0 = 0\n\nCalculating the subtraction:\n\n1/x - 1/x + 2/y - (-6/y) + 3/z - (-5/z) = 0\n\nSimplify:\n\n0 + (2/y + 6/y) + (3/z + 5/z) = 0\n\nWhich is 8/y + 8/z = 0\n\nSo, 8/y + 8/z = 0. Let me divide both sides by 8 to simplify:\n\n1/y + 1/z = 0\n\nSo that tells me that 1/y = -1/z, which means z = -y. Interesting. So z and y are negatives of each other. Let me note that:\n\nz = -y  ...(3)\n\nOkay, now that I have a relationship between z and y, maybe I can substitute this back into one of the original equations to find another relationship. Let's take equation (1) again:\n\n1/x + 2/y + 3/z = 0\n\nSubstitute z = -y from equation (3):\n\n1/x + 2/y + 3/(-y) = 0\n\nSimplify the third term:\n\n1/x + 2/y - 3/y = 0\n\nCombine the terms in y:\n\n1/x + (2/y - 3/y) = 0\n\nWhich is 1/x - 1/y = 0\n\nSo, 1/x = 1/y, which implies x = y. So x equals y. Let me write that:\n\nx = y 