} = (s - t)^{2}\n    \\]\n\n    Consequently,\n\n    \\[\n    \\sum_{k=1}^{n} x_{k}^{2} - \\left( \\sum_{k=1}^{n} x_{k} \\right)^{2} = n - (s - t)^2\n    \\]\n\n    Given $s + t = n$, the value $(s - t)^2$ is minimized when $s = t$ or as close as possible to being equal, meaning $\\left| s - t \\right| \\leq 1$. Therefore:\n\n    \\[\n    (s - t)^2 \\leq (n - 2 \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{2} \\right\\rfloor)^2\n    \\]\n\n    Hence,\n\n    \\[\n    \\sum_{k=1}^{n} x_{k}^{2} - \\left( \\sum_{k=1}^{n} x_{k} \\right)^{2} \\leq n - (n - 2 \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{2} \\right\\rfloor) = 2 \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{2} \\right\\rfloor\n    \\]\n\n    The equality holds when there are exactly $\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{2} \\right\\rfloor$ ones and $\\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{2} \\right\\rceil$ negative ones.\n\n4. **Returning to the original problem**: Let us rotate the coordinate system so that $\\sum_{k=1}^{n} z_k^2 \\in \\mathbb{R}$ and $\\sum_{k=1}^{n} z_k^2 \\geq 0$. Assuming $z_k = x_k + i y_k \\, (1 \\leq k \\leq n)$, we have:\n\n    \\[\n    \\sum_{k=1}^{n} z_{k}^2 = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} (x_k + i y_k)^2 = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} (x_k^2 - y_k^2) + 2i \\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{n} x_k y_k \\right) \n    \\]\n\n    Thus:\n\n    \\[\n    \\left| \\sum_{k=1}^{n} z_{k} \\right|^2 = \\left| \\left( \\sum_{k=1}^{n} x_k \\right) + i \\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{n} y_k \\right)\\right|^2 = \\left( \\sum_{k=1}^{n} x_k \\right)^2 + \\left( \\sum_{k=1}^{n} y_k \\right)^2\n    \\]\n\n    Therefore:\n\n    \\[\n    \\left| \\sum_{k=1}^{n} z_{k}^{2} \\right| - \\left| \\sum_{k=1}^{n} z_{k} \\right|^2 = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} (x_k^2 - y_k^2) - \\left( \\left( \\sum_{k=1}^{n} x_k \\right)^2 + \\left( \\sum_{k=1}^{n} y_k \\right)^2 \\right)\n    \\]\n\n    Applying the lemma:\n\n    \\[\n    \\left| \\sum_{k=1}^{n} z_{k}^2 \\right| - \\left| \\sum_{k=1}^{n} z_{k} \\right|^2 \\leq \\sum_{k=1}^{n} x_k^2 - \\left( \\sum_{k=1}^{n} x_k \\right)^2 \\leq 2 \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{2} \\right\\rfloor\n    \\]\n\n    This maximal value i